where we follow the notation of [26].33 3 In particular, in contrast to the main text, both graviton momenta, $p_{1}$ and $p_{2}$ , are taken outgoing. The first diagram constructs all the terms with master integrals, $\mathcal{K}_{1}$ and $\mathcal{K}_{3}$ , while the second diagram provides the terms with $\mathcal{K}_{2}$ and $\mathcal{K}_{3}$ . The union of the two graphs means keeping only one copy of the overlapping $\mathcal{K}_{3}$ term and adding it together with the $\mathcal{K}_{1}$ and $\mathcal{K}_{2}$ terms. After summation over the intermediate graviton state in the first graph, we get the integrand,

$$ \displaystyle A_{\rm comp}^{(1,a)}(p_{1},p_{2},v) \displaystyle=\Big(\int{d^{D}\ell\over(2\pi)^{D}}\delta(2Mv{\cdot}(\ell+p_{1})){1\over\ell^{2}}\sum_{h_{\ell}}A_{\rm comp}(p_{1},\ell,v)A_{\rm comp}(-\ell,p_{2},v) \displaystyle=\int{d^{D}\ell\over(2\pi)^{D}}\delta(2Mv{\cdot}(\ell+p_{1})){1\over\ell^{2}}\Bigg(-\frac{(D-3)M^{4}\left(\ell{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}v\right)^{2}\left(\ell{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}v\right)^{2}}{4(D-2)\ell{\cdot}p_{1}\ell{\cdot}p_{2}\left(p_{1}{\cdot}v\right)^{4}} \displaystyle+\frac{M^{4}v{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}v\ell{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}v\ell{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}v}{2\ell{\cdot}p_{1}\ell{\cdot}p_{2}\left(p_{1}{\cdot}v\right)^{2}}-\frac{M^{4}\left(v{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}v\right)^{2}}{4\ell{\cdot}p_{1}\ell{\cdot}p_{2}}\Bigg), $$

which is manifestly gauge-invariant as $f^{\mu\nu}_{i}\equiv p^{\mu}_{i}\varepsilon^{\nu}_{i}-\varepsilon^{\mu}_{i}p^{\nu}_{i}$ . For the second graph, the integrand is

$$ \displaystyle A_{\rm comp}^{(1,b)}(p_{1},p_{2},v) \displaystyle=\int{d^{D}\ell\over(2\pi)^{D}}\delta(2Mv{\cdot}(\ell+p_{1})){1\over\ell^{2}} \displaystyle\times\Big(\sum_{h_{\ell+p_{1}},h_{\ell-p_{2}}}A_{3}(p_{1}+\ell,v)A_{\rm 3}(p_{2}-\ell,v)A_{\rm GR}(p_{1},-\ell-p_{1},\ell-p_{2},p_{2})\Big)\,, $$

where $A_{\rm GR}$ is the graviton amplitude. We note that the manifest gauge-invariant form of the integrand can also be obtained by the gauge-invariant double copy form of $A_{\rm GR}$ [153].

From the glued integrand, we perform the IBP reduction and get

$$ \displaystyle A_{\rm comp}^{(1,a)}(p_{1},p_{2},v)=M^{3}\left(v_{1}{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}v_{1}\right)^{2} \displaystyle\times\left(\frac{\mathcal{K}_{3}\left(3-2y^{2}\right)}{3(y-1)^{2}}+\frac{\mathcal{K}_{1}(3-4y)}{72(y-1)^{2}\omega^{4}}+\frac{\mathcal{K}_{1}(6-5y)}{24(y-1)^{2}\omega^{4}\epsilon}-\frac{\mathcal{K}_{3}y(31y-36)\epsilon}{9(y-1)^{2}}\right) \displaystyle+M^{3}\left(p_{1}{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}v_{1}\right)^{2}\left(p_{2}{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}v_{1}\right)^{2} \displaystyle\times\left(\frac{\mathcal{K}_{3}\left(10y^{2}+8y-3\right)\epsilon}{72(y-1)^{4}\omega^{4}}-\frac{\mathcal{K}_{1}(17y+4)}{576(y-1)^{4}\omega^{8}}+\frac{\mathcal{K}_{3}y(y+2)}{12(y-1)^{4}\omega^{4}}+\frac{\mathcal{K}_{1}(y+2)}{96(y-1)^{4}\omega^{8}\epsilon}\right) \displaystyle+M^{3}v_{1}{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}v_{1}p_{1}{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}v_{1}p_{2}{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}v_{1} \displaystyle\times\left(\frac{\mathcal{K}_{3}\left(13y^{2}-29y+9\right)\epsilon}{9(y-1)^{3}\omega^{2}}+\frac{\mathcal{K}_{1}(7-2y)}{72(y-1)^{3}\omega^{6}}+\frac{2\mathcal{K}_{3}(y-2)y}{3(y-1)^{3}\omega^{2}}+\frac{\mathcal{K}_{1}(y-2)}{12(y-1)^{3}\omega^{6}\epsilon}\right)\,, $$

and

$$ \displaystyle A_{\rm comp}^{(1,b)}(p_{1},p_{2},v) \displaystyle=M^{3}{\mathcal{K}_{2}\over 2}\Big(-\frac{\left(y^{3}-y^{2}+39y+9\right)\left(p_{1}{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}v\right)^{2}\left(p_{2}{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}v\right)^{2}}{192\omega^{6}(y-1)^{4}} \displaystyle+\frac{\left(y^{3}-23y^{2}+27y+27\right)v{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}vp_{1}{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}vp_{2}{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}v}{48\omega^{4}(y-1)^{3}} \displaystyle-\frac{\left(y^{3}-45y^{2}+15y+45\right)\left(v{\cdot}f_{1}{\cdot}f_{2}{\cdot}v\right)^{2}}{48\omega^{2}(y-1)^{2}}\Big)+(\mathcal{K}_{3}-\text{term})\,, $$

where the $(\mathcal{K}_{3}-\text{term})$ is the same as the one in eq. (D.4). These expressions confirm the result reported in the main text.

